In this equation:
*   S<sub>product(s) is the standard entropy of the product.
*   S<sub>reactant(s) is the standard entropy of the reactant.
ΔS = ΣnS<sub>product(s) - ΣnS<sub>rantant(s)

Given the reaction:

2 PbS(s) + 3 O₂(g) → 2 PbO(s) + 2  (ΔS = ΣnS<sub>product - ΣnS<sub>rantant

