4. Solvent effects: The solvent used in the synthesis or study of the complex can have an impact on the coordination geometry. Some solvents can coordinate to the iron (III) ion, potentially leading to changes in the geometry.

5. Temperature and pressure: Changes in temperature and pressure can affect the coordination geometry by altering the relative energies of different geometries, potentially leading to a change in the preferred geometry.
