In summary, the optimal ratio of TiO2 nanoparticles and graphene oxide in a composite material for high-performance dye-sensitized solar cells depends on the specific application and desired properties of the solar cell. However, research has shown that incorporating a small amount of GO (1-2 wt%) into the TiO2 matrix can improve the overall efficiency and stability of the solar cell. Further research and optimization may be required to determine the ideal ratio for a specific application.
