We have $a_n = 19 + (n-1)d$.
Then $a_5 = 19 + (5-1)d = 19 + 4d$ and $a_6 = 19 + (6-1)d = 19 + 5d$.
Since $a_5 \geq 0$ and $a_6 < 0$, we have
$19 + 4d \geq 0 \implies 4d \geq -19 \implies d \geq -\frac{19}{4} = -4.75$
$19 + 5d < 0 \implies 5d < -19 \implies d < -\frac{19}{5} = -3.8$
Since $d$ is an integer, we have $d \in \mathbb{Z}$ such that $-4.75 \leq d < -3.8$.
The only integer that satisfies this condition is $d = -4$.
