The magnitude of $a_n$ is given by
$$ |a_n| = \sqrt{(n - 2016)^2 + (n + 13)^2} = \sqrt{n^2 - 4032n + 2016^2 + n^2 + 26n + 13^2} = \sqrt{2n^2 - 4006n + 2016^2 + 169} = \sqrt{2n^2 - 4006n + 4064256 + 169} = \sqrt{2n^2 - 4006n + 4064425} $
To find the value of $n$ that minimizes $|a_n|$, we can find the derivative of the function $f(n) = 2n^2 - 4006n + 4064425$ and set it to 0.
$f'(n) = 4n - 4006 = 0 \Rightarrow n = \frac{4006}{4} = \frac{2003}{2} = 1001.5$
