$$ \left| \left(\frac{1}{3}\sin t + \cos t\right) e^{-t/2} \right| \le \left| \frac{1}{3}\sin t \right| |e^{-t/2}| + |\cos t| |e^{-t2/2}| \text{ and } \left| \frac{1}{3} \sin t \right| \text{ and } |\cos t| \text{ are bounded. } $$
Since $e^{-t/2} \to 0$ as $t \to \infty$, we have
$$ \left(\frac{1}{3}\sin t + \cos t\right) e^{-t/2} \to 0 \text{ as } t \to \infty. $$
Thus,
