</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The refractive index (n) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (c) to the speed of light in a medium (v):

n = c / v

We are given that the speed of light in the plasma is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum.  Therefore, v = 0.680c.

Substituting this into the equation for the refractive index:

n = c / (0.680c) = 1 / 0.680 ≈ 1.47

So, the refractive index for the yellow light in the plasma is approximately ** 1.47**.
